From c127647f95e60ed9cc3e251c648ca0e3e82d10ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Dolbeau <romain@dolbeau.org>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 22:23:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hw/m68k/sun3mmu: let the MMU reach the SCSI registers

sun3mmu_get_physical_address checks the translated physical address
against a list of what exists on this machine, and turns anything else
into a bus-error timeout before the access is dispatched.  The onboard
SCSI at obio 0x140000 is not on that list, so it is unreachable through
the MMU however well it is modelled: the PROM's probe writes one word to
the board, takes a bus error, and reports "Device not found" without
ever having read a register.

Add the range.  It is 40 bytes rather than the 32 the register block is
usually described as, because the driver that serves both the onboard
and the VME board writes the VME-only registers unconditionally and the
3/60 PROM is one such driver - si_iv_am at 0x1e and fifo_cnt_hi at 0x20
are written before anything else happens.

Signed-off-by: Romain Dolbeau <romain@dolbeau.org>
---
 hw/m68k/sun3mmu.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/m68k/sun3mmu.c b/hw/m68k/sun3mmu.c
index a0192b5677..e495f8ee98 100644
--- a/hw/m68k/sun3mmu.c
+++ b/hw/m68k/sun3mmu.c
@@ -413,6 +413,9 @@ static bool is_valid_sun3_phys(hwaddr p, ram_addr_t ram_size)
     if (p >= 0x0FF20000 && p <= 0x0FF201FF) {
         return true; /* LANCE Am7990 */
     }
+    if (p >= 0x0FF40000 && p <= 0x0FF40027) {
+        return true; /* si SCSI: NCR 5380, Am9516 UDC and FIFO */
+    }
     if (p >= 0x0FE60000 && p <= 0x0FE6003F) {
         return true; /* Timer */
     }
